profile_view.description:
These are the values the profile carries. Home Assistant scales them to every cover that follows it, in proportion to that cover's height.

{values}
Covers following it: {covers}

calibration_actions.description:
What is kept for this cover:

{values}
**What you have to do**: choose what to do with it. “Measure it again” runs the guided calibration on this cover and replaces what is here; “Delete” hands it back to the configuration file, if you use one.

calibration_view.description:
This is what the integration keeps for this cover:

{values}
The keys listed here beat the ones written in the configuration file, if you use one; the ones that do not appear go on coming from the file, from the profile or from the defaults.

summary_basic.description:
**Curtain travel**: {height}

**Where these values go**: if you save, they stay inside Home Assistant, here under Configure → Calibrations, and the cover uses them at once instead of the ones in the configuration file, if you use one. From that same screen you can look at them again, correct them by hand or delete them at any time.

If you would rather write them into the file yourself, the equivalent snippet is below: copy it before you close this, because without saving nothing is kept.

{yaml}
The accuracy has not been checked yet. “Improve the accuracy” measures four more points and shows the gap in centimetres.

**What you have to do**: save, or spend another two minutes and four tape readings.

unknown_keys.description:
`{path}` contains {count} key(s) the integration does not know; they are ignored:

{keys}

Remove or correct them, then reload the integration. You can dismiss this notice if the keys are intentional.
